8)","type":{"id":"505","text":"Goal","abbreviation":"goal"},"clock":{"displayValue":"1:35"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"13"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"5149204","displayName":"Gabe Perreault","shortName":"G. Perreault"},"type":"scorer"},{"athlete":{"id":"2562637","displayName":"Mika Zibanejad","shortName":"M. Zibanejad"},"type":"assister"},{"athlete":{"id":"4697382","displayName":"Alexis Lafreniere","shortName":"A. Lafreniere"},"type":"assister"}]},{"id":"401892664000000690","scoringPlay":false,"scoreValue":0,"awayScore":1,"homeScore":0,"text":"Berkly Catton faceoff won against Will Cuylle","type":{"id":"502","text":"Face Off","abbreviation":"faceoff"},"clock":{"displayValue":"1:35"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"124292"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"5216877","displayName":"Berkly Catton","shortName":"B. Catton"},"type":"face-off-winner"},{"athlete":{"id":"4697468","displayName":"Will Cuylle","shortName":"W. Cuylle"}}]},{"id":"401892664000000970","scoringPlay":false,"scoreValue":0,"awayScore":1,"homeScore":0,"text":"Giveaway by Pavel Dorofeyev","type":{"id":"1402","text":"Giveaway","abbreviation":"giveaway"},"clock":{"displayValue":"1:44"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"13"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"4587588","displayName":"Pavel Dorofeyev","shortName":"P. Dorofeyev"},"type":"giver"}]}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"7224","fullName":"Climate Pledge Arena","address":{"city":"Seattle","state":"WA","country":"USA"},"grass":false,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/nhl/day/7224.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day"]}]},"attendance":17151,"officials":[{"fullName":"Ryan Gibbons","displayName":"Ryan Gibbons","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Scott Cherrey","displayName":"Scott Cherrey","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Cody Beach","displayName":"Cody Beach","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Chris Rooney","displayName":"Chris Rooney","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"Rangers hold off the Kraken 4-3 for their 3rd straight victory","description":"— Gabe Perreault, Tye Kartye and Jaroslav Chmelar scored in the first period and the New York Rangers held off the Seattle Kraken 4-3 on Saturday for their third straight victory.","story":"SEATTLE -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5149204/gabe-perreault\">Gabe Perreault</a>, <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4588750/tye-kartye\">Tye Kartye</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5188348/jaroslav-chmelar\">Jaroslav Chmelar</a> scored in the first period and the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/nyr/new-york-rangers\">New York Rangers</a> held off the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/sea/seattle-kraken\">Seattle Kraken</a> 4-3 on Saturday for their third straight victory. \n\n\r\n              Pavel Dorofeyevalos also scored for the Rangers (10-7-1), and Alexis Lafrenière and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/2562637/mika-zibanejad\">Mika Zibanejad</a> each had two assists.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3069266/joonas-korpisalo\">Joonas Korpisalo</a> stopped 25 shots in his Rangers debut. Acquired from Boston in July, he had been on injured reserve because of a foot infection.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4565223/kaapo-kakko\">Kaapo Kakko</a>, <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5032/jordan-eberle\">Jordan Eberle</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3904189/vince-dunn\">Vince Dunn</a> scored for Seattle (9-6-1) in the final period. Berkley Catton had two assists, extending his points streak to a career-high eight games. \n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3942073/joey-daccord\">Joey Daccord</a> was pulled for <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5657/philipp-grubauer\">Philipp Grubauer</a> after giving up three goals in the first 14 minutes. Grubauer stopped 15 shots.\n\n\r\n              Chmelar scored off a rebound to make it 3-0, tapping it in past Daccord after he failed to corral <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5188370/noah-laba\">Noah Laba</a>'s shot attempt. \n\n\r\n              Dorofeyev extended the Rangers lead to 4-0 with a nifty backhand to beat Grubauer with seven minutes remaining in the second period. It was Dorofeyev's third goal over his last four games. \n\n\r\n              Kakko scored on a wraparound goal at 1:50 of the third period. \n\n\r\n              Eberle scored inside the crease for his fifth goal of the season. Dunn's slap shot trimmed lead to a goal with 4:58 remaining. \n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Rangers: At Edmonton on Monday night. \n\n\r\n              Kraken: Head to Finland for the NHL Global Series, playing two games against Carolina starting Thursday.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-11-08T00:50:35Z"}}